nodecode-music-jam is a rewrite of vdimarco's vdimarco/agent-music-jam:

  https://github.com/vdimarco/agent-music-jam
  commit 009c918b89e7ba98550de0755b47d1e5e7bc96a0
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Agent Music Jam contributors (LICENSE)

Rewritten in Common Lisp: the four roles and their controls, the local pattern
rules note for note, the session shape, the arrangement queue that holds every
change until a bar boundary, per-musician undo, save and restore, the standard
MIDI writer, and the ten tools the original registered (jam_start, jam_inspect,
jam_stop, jam_direct, jam_configure, jam_schedule, jam_undo, jam_save,
jam_restore, jam_export) with the same names and arguments. The loopback page
is reimplemented: the same four cards, transport, clock and keyboard, with the
band synthesized in the page's own Web Audio and every API call carrying the
token the address holds.

Left out, and why: the original's two model planners (a conductor and one
planner a role, run as Hermes child sessions) are gone, so a direction is read
by the original's own stand-alone rule vocabulary instead of a model; the
browser's recorded WAV download went with them, and jam_export writes MIDI.
Hermes's profile-scoped state is replaced by the Nodecode home. The page is
served by the cell's own listener on 127.0.0.1 rather than the gateway's port.
